==English==

===Etymology===
From Latin [[proboscis]], from Greek [[προβοσκίς]] "elephant's trunk," literally "means for taking food," from [[προ]] "forward" + [[βόσκειν]] "to nourish, feed," from [[βόσκεσςθαι]] "graze, be fed," from the root *bot (cf. [[βοτάνη]] "grass, fodder); more at [[botany]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/proʊˈbɒsɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|es|pl2=proboscides|pl3=probosci}}

# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} An elongated tube from the head or connected to the mouth, of an animal. 
## The tubular feeding and sucking organ of certain [[invertebrate]]s like [[insect]]s, [[worm]]s and [[mollusc]]s.
## The trunk of an [[elephant]].
# Informally, a large human nose.

